+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }` and
+answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (`dishes` is the sum of `qty`). Each
+dish sold consumes its recipe's ingredients for `qty` portions, with ledger
+`ref` `sale:<ticket>`. Tickets already imported are skipped. If any row is
+invalid or an item runs out, nothing is imported and the `bad_request`
+message names the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers, per item with
+any use, `{ itemId, name, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical
+from sales sold on those days, actual from `consume` movements on those days,
+`difference = actual - theoretical`.
